# How to cite QUMO. GitHub reads this file and shows "Cite this repository".
# QUMO has no tagged release yet: also state the commit hash you used.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QUMO in your research, please cite it using this metadata and state the commit hash you used."
type: software
title: "QUMO"
abstract: >-
  QUMO is a hardware-neutral, AI-native quantum software stack written in Mojo:
  circuit IR with OpenQASM 2/3, a vendor-neutral compiler, state-vector,
  stabilizer, Pauli-frame and density-matrix simulators, GPU kernels, quantum
  error correction, fault-tolerant programming, an algorithms library, a
  command line tool and an MCP server for LLM agents. Research prototype.
authors:
  - given-names: "Ismael"
    family-names: "Faro Sertage"
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ANFAIA/QUMO"
url: "https://github.com/ANFAIA/QUMO"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum circuit simulation
  - quantum compilation
  - quantum error correction
  - OpenQASM
  - Mojo
